Key Discussion Points
Data Ingestion Flow
Data is ingested from Kafka into the MSK landing S3 bucket (with subdirectories for non‑prod, prod, and topics).
Production data is stored in the prod folder; ~1010 topics exist, with 8 currently loaded.
Issues remain with MAXI_HLTH_CLM and MAXI_HLTH_UWR due to JSON key space issues.
Orchestrator DAG
Runs hourly (24 times per day).
Uses a master JSON configuration file containing topic paths, scheduling windows, and all other parameters.
Sync types: FRO (full load at topic start) and INU (incremental load thereafter).
Staging Process
Files from S3 are copied into Snowflake staging tables.
Incremental loads append to stage tables; mirror tables process only incremental data in INU mode by creating view on the stage tables.
Batching mechanism: files grouped into ~1000 per batch; checkpoint tables track batch completion to resume from failures.
Performance: ~1–1.5 minutes per batch of 1000 files; 100 batches (~100,000 files) take ~1h 40m.
Mirror Tables
Wrapper procedure in Snowflake processes staged JSON into mirror tables.
Variant keys define which nested JSON paths to flatten into tables.
Metadata differences (new JSON attributes) are logged and notified via email; updates required in configuration.
Metadata Handling
Metadata tables store file details (filename, key_path, key_type, ...)
Logs provide detailed statistics on staging and ingestion success rates.
